WEBVTT

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.940
<b>Book 2: The Snow Continues to Fall</b>

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:07.000
<b>Episode 6: Confidential File 623, Daybreak</b>

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.980
Tsuki-san, do you hate Onee-chan?

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.680
Not at all. I love her, in fact.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.830
She's stronger—and in more 
danger—than anyone I know.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.990
It makes her hard to leave alone.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:23.970
You don't need to understand. 
Just remember this.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:27.700
It's very hard to live a lie.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.250
But when lived to its fullest,

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.100
a lie becomes more 
meaningful than the truth.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.730
If you and Yukimura-kun wish 
for it, you can leave,

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:40.200
for a place where it'll be 
just the two of you,

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.890
with no one getting in the way.

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:44.480
Just us?

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.060
So, are you interested 
in what I have to say?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.990
<i>This drug causes death ten 
seconds after ingestion.</i>

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.360
I need to do this right...

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.530
<i>Once she stops breathing, 
check the time right away.</i>

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:06.930
I need to!

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.280
I say she'll die, but it's more 
like a near-death state.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:13.000
She'll only <i>look</i> like she's 
dead, in other words.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.710
And after three hours, her heart 
will start to beat normally again.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.920
So she won't die?

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:21.650
Right. That's what makes it difficult.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:25.270
You need to convince everyone 
she's dead during those three hours,

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:28.450
or there's no point to any of this.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:33.690
At around 1:30 PM, a messenger boy will show up.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:36.890
Hello!

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:41.700
Huh?

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:45.880
Excuse me...

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.040
<i>You'll need to tell him 
that Yukimura-kun is dead.</i>

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.020
<i>And shortly after that...</i>

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:01.820
<i>A man in glasses will arrive.</i>

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:06.550
Excuse me. I'm a friend of Yukimura-kun's.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.850
Where is she?

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:11.740
<i>Tell him she's dead, too.</i>

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:15.140
<i>Do not ask a single question.</i>

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.240
She does seem to be dead.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:27.700
Could you explain what happened again?

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:32.130
She grabbed her chest all 
of a sudden... like it hurt...

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:33.410
And then...

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:37.840
<i>You'll need to put on quite a performance.</i>

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:43.420
<i>Because if you can't, 
he's going to kill you.</i>

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:00.770
You have my condolences 
for your sudden loss.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:12.580
I'll handle the arrangements for 
her funeral and report her death.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.650
<i>When a member of the 
organization dies suddenly,</i>

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:17.890
<i>they make sure to deal with it internally.</i>

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:22.810
<i>He'll come up with some sort of 
excuse to run off with her body.</i>

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:24.450
Onee-chan...

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:28.710
<i>You need to go with her, though.</i>

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:31.860
<i>If you can't, the game will be over.</i>

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.030
Onee-chan!

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:40.920
Onee-chan...

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.890
Hop in the back, miss.

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:49.860
Okay...

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:55.620
<i>Yukimura-kun was special 
to the man with the glasses.</i>

00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:00.120
<i>And since she cared about you, 
there's reason to believe</i>

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:04.280
<i>he won't kill you too easily 
just because you're in the way.</i>

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:10.590
If things go smoothly, this should all 
take about an hour and a half.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:13.010
I might die?

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:15.770
If it happens, it happens.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.980
Now, this next part is crucial.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:25.260
You'll arrive at the graveyard. 
The cleaners will get the burial underway.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:44.900
Death is just an endless sleep, eh?

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:02.810
<i>There won't be much air inside the casket.</i>

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:07.390
<i>If she's still inside it when 
she wakes up, she'll suffocate.</i>

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:09.740
<i>Meaning she'll die for real.</i>

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.090
<i>Before time is up, you have to get her out.</i>

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:15.400
If things go in your favor,

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.910
you'll be reunited in the land of the living.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:23.090
Then you just need to escape Tokyo 
and continue to play family.

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:24.960
Do you really think I can do that?

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.010
It doesn't matter what anyone thinks.

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:30.050
You have to be dead-set on <i>making</i> it happen.

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:33.490
<i>The truth isn't important.</i>

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:36.890
<i>It's how things look, and how you 
choose to make them look.</i>

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:50.620
<i>Fifteen minutes left...</i>

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:52.680
You don't want to leave her?

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:54.980
Not yet.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:07:59.410
Is that it?

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:01.080
Yes, sir.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.200
I need you on another matter. Come with me.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.010
Yes, sir.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.500
I forgot to mention this,

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:11.300
but someone from an orphanage will 
be along to collect you tomorrow.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:14.640
You can decide what to do next with them.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.090
Okay...

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:18.890
I'll have a car come and pick you up later.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:22.680
Until then... you're free to remain here.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:54.120
I've always thought this...

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.040
Have you noticed how Jin 
Kuzuhara's fashion is so...

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:58.050
Oh, I know what you mean!

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.510
It's off!

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:08.070
Granted, it doesn't matter how 
they dress once they're naked.

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:10.070
The important things 
are their face and body.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.730
You're such an animal.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:13.410
Why, thank you!

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:17.900
So, how about you?

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:18.740
Excuse me?

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:21.240
Your type of man.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:24.200
I don't really have one.

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:29.780
Do you seriously never feel 
like you just need somebody?

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:30.960
I don't.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:34.550
It's a little simplistic to assume 
Yukimura-kun would feel that way

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.120
just because you do.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:41.680
As for me... I can see the appeal.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.430
You can?

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:46.380
What do I seem like to you?

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:50.150
You can't just write human 
feelings off as being good or bad.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:55.880
There are times when life feels so 
meaningless, so hard, so awful...

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:57.840
you just want someone to cling to.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:02.510
That's what I mean when I talk 
about needing somebody.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:04.200
Really?

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:08.040
That look screams, "I have no idea 
what you're talking about."

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:13.880
Indulging in a bit of warmth so that 
you can forget, even for a moment...

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:16.590
Forget about everything.

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:20.540
It's impossible to forget about everything.

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:22.780
I personally wouldn't want to forget.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:28.000
This is why I say I hate you.

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:35.940
See, she's crying.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:38.080
And it's all your fault.

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:40.350
Wait, when did you...

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:43.410
Look at my darling little baby.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.120
There, there, it's okay.

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:52.000
Onee-chan...

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:54.820
Asahi?

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:59.970
We're real sisters now, huh?

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:05.560
Because I killed Yukimura.

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:13.150
Yukimura-kun is dead.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.650
Goodbye.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.120
<i>I'm...</i>

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:27.620
Onee-chan!

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:33.360
Asahi?

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:38.000
Where am I?

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:42.270
Yuki's dead.

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:44.700
Yuki the Killer is dead now!

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:47.790
I killed her.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:49.850
What are you talking about?

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:53.860
You've died and been reborn, Onee-chan!

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:57.820
<i>That must've been it...</i>

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:00.080
Run with me!

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:04.250
But... they won't let us 
get away with this...

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:08.240
Onee-chan, you understand, 
right? We have to run!

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:11.520
But where could we even run?

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.380
Asakura Temple, Iwai Prefecture

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.420
We'd need a boat to get here.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:28.300
I bought two tickets this morning, 
with the money you gave me before.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:31.140
If they find out, they're gonna kill me!

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:35.240
Please! Help me one more time!

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.070
Hang in there a bit longer!

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:48.530
That's it... A bit more...

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:49.660
<b>Detective Kazuaki Tanaka, 
City Police</b>

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:53.690
The body of an Englishman 
was found in an abandoned car.

00:12:53.690 --> 00:12:56.540
The culprit is Makoto Tsukishiro.

00:12:57.310 --> 00:13:00.920
We know you were treating her here.

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:03.260
What is she after?

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.680
Couldn't tell ya.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.180
Really?

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:19.690
I'm sure neither of us wants 
to waste our time...

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:20.570
Hold it!

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:26.430
I saw some kind of blue medicine.

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:28.780
It was in an instrument case.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.520
Go on.

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:39.250
I'll tell ya what I know, 
but it ain't gonna matter in the end.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:43.850
I can tell you're not regular police.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:45.760
And what does that matter?

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:49.790
The way the administration runs things 
isn't gonna fly forever. It just can't.

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:55.230
Sooner or later, it's gonna fall apart. 
Just a question of when.

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:58.400
Runnin' around crushin' the opposition

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.980
isn't gonna make a difference 
in the long run!

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:03.030
You've gotta realize that!

00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:07.130
A world where the logical 
answer is enough...

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:10.880
What I would give to live 
in a place like that.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.680
Now, keep talking.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:23.440
Congratulations! She looks 
just like you, ma'am!

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:40.060
Asahi!

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:45.640
I'm okay!

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:49.710
Asahi...

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:50.960
What is it?

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:53.230
We don't have to run together.

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:56.830
If I surrender to the organization—

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:58.040
No!

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:01.540
You can't do that!

00:15:01.990 --> 00:15:04.970
Onee-chan, you're going to come live with me!

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.440
Are you sure he went this way?

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.190
Yes, let's find him.

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:06.860
I'm sure you'll be happy 
about what you find.

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:16.220
It's the port!

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:19.390
We're almost out of here!

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:23.840
We leave Tokyo... and then what?

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:28.840
You won't have to kill anyone else, 
and we can live together forever.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:31.540
I don't have to kill anymore?

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:35.550
But... can we really find a life like that?

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:37.890
Your name.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.810
I'm Asahi Nakamura.

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:44.520
What about you, Onee-chan?

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:51.010
I'm...

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.530
Sawa.

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:58.990
Sawa Karasumori.

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:01.540
Sawa-oneechan...

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:04.600
What a cute name!

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:08.550
The head of state and commander-in-chief,

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:11.550
Shogun Yoshinobu Tokugawa-sama has arrived.

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:14.510
All in attendance, bow.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.510
Raise your heads.

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:28.020
This cabinet meeting will now begin.

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:30.480
Minister for Foreign Affairs, your report.

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:33.160
I'm sorry to report...

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:37.060
The French have refused to budge 
on the issue of the mining rights

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:40.020
to the coal in the ceded territory 
of Takashima in Kyushu,

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:43.110
and have been exerting pressure via trade,

00:17:43.110 --> 00:17:45.300
making the state of business 
take a turn for the worse...

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:56.260
The shogun has declared a raise in taxes 
will account for the difference in revenue.

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:57.360
Yes, sir.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:17:59.720
Next, the Minister of the Interior.

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:04.770
It's my pleasure to announce the leader of 
the anti-government organization, Kuchinawa,

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:09.160
has been eliminated at the hands 
of the shogun's personal covert agents.

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:12.840
Sadly, insurrections have continued 
to break out throughout the country,

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:18.740
with the incidents in Yamaguchi and 
Niigata apparently having English backing,

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:21.900
as verified by the intelligence service.

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:26.430
For the time being, maintain 
order as you have been.

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:30.750
If the police are insufficient, 
you may use the military.

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:33.550
I assume you have no 
objections, Minister of War?

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:35.000
By the shogun's will.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:37.990
Next we'll hear from the Minister 
of Communications and Transport—

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:52.480
Let's hear your report.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:19:00.490
We'll be obtaining the blood formula 
created by the traitor Janome shortly.

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:02.920
The traitor, eh?

00:19:02.920 --> 00:19:05.420
I'm sure he would call us the same.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:08.060
You jest, sir.

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:10.210
The researchers are ready to work.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:13.200
Once we have this formula,

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:15.960
we'll be able to produce 
a more refined version...

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:19.970
which will resolve both this foreign 
posturing and these internal squabbles.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:22.470
I will make sure to deliver it.

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:25.990
And you've secured the original 
source as well, haven't you?

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:30.500
Bringing in the girl with the blue blood...

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:33.280
Looking back now, that was 
quite the accomplishment.

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:36.260
Just don't forget...

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:40.540
No path is open to you 
except one caked in blood.

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:10.120
Thank you.

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:14.100
You bastards!

00:20:14.590 --> 00:20:16.360
What do you think you're doing?!

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:18.160
If you're going to kill us, just do it!

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:19.980
<b>Down with Tokugawa 
 Rise up</b>

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:19.980
Our lives aren't what matters!

00:20:19.980 --> 00:20:22.600
Shut your criminal mouths.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:55.460
<b>Down with Tokugawa
Rise up</b>

00:20:55.460 --> 00:21:00.930
<b>Rise up</b>

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:08.450
Two Days Later in Iwai Prefecture

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:07.900
Can we really... live in a place like this?

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:10.900
It'll be okay.

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:14.890
It doesn't matter where we are, 
as long as I'm with you, Onee-chan.
